Subject: Hijack the online multiplayer menu to the debug LAN multiplayer
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a

Retail never calls NetworkSession::InitializeLAN. Under the explicit
MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_LAN admission, Main Menu's Online item starts
the LAN session and pushes the original lobby (scene 24, NetworkStartScene)
instead of the DWC login; its back button shuts the session down and returns
to Main Menu. The lobby and the two network draft scenes leave their gated
blocks, split only at case boundaries; hub, login, Mii selection and every
DWC scene keep their gates. The LAN session starts ranked matches, but
without a stats server or the online ranking overlay (scene 93): after each
game the post-game results continue the series directly, like an unranked
network game, and a finished series returns to Main Menu like a friendly
match instead of pushing the unadmitted online hub. The online lobby does not
exist outside NET_MODE_ONLINE, so a peer lost during the draft (captain,
sidekick or matchmaking draft scene) ends the LAN session instead of closing
the online lobby's connections, and its popup returns to Main Menu instead
of the unadmitted online menus. The lobby is entered from Main Menu without
the online camera transition, so that return is the lobby back button's plain
Main Menu push, not TransitionOnlineMatchToMainMenu (which pops a camera this
flow never pushed and crashed from the sidekick draft).

The admission prints the original DC_NETWORK debug channel to stderr.
SHOnlinePlayerCount's button context words are narrowed through
std::uintptr_t natively.

